    #     msgpack \
    #     scipy \
    #     flask \
    #     waitress \
    #     biopython

    # # Install the modified evo2 package over the base image version.
    # # --no-deps ensures we don't break the base image's PyTorch/Vortex installations
    # echo "Installing modified Evo 2 package..."
    # python3 -m pip install -e /opt/evo2-predictor/evo2 --no-deps --force-reinstall
    
    # # Set permissions to access all directories
    # echo "Setting permissions for directories and script..."
    # chmod -R 755 /opt/evo2-predictor/

    # # Verification: Ensure the track function imports successfully against base dependencies
    # echo "Running verification checks..."
    # python3 -c "import evo2, torch; from evo2.scoring import score_sequences_track; print('Evo 2 + track import OK')"
    
    # # Verification: Ensure weights are present
    # test -s /opt/evo2-predictor/weights/evo2_7b.pt && echo "Evo 2 Weights Verified"

%runscript
    exec python3 /opt/evo2-predictor/predictor_RestAPI.py "$@"

%startscript
    exec python3 /opt/evo2-predictor/predictor_RestAPI.py "$@"

%labels
    Authors "Ishika Luthra"
    game_schema_version "1.0"
    Description "Self-contained RESTful Evo 2 7B Predictor for the GAME framework"

%help
    Evo 2 (7B) Predictor for the Genomic API for Model Evaluation (GAME) framework.

    This container serves a Flask-based REST API that wraps the Evo 2 7B DNA language model (Brixi et al., Nature 2026; Arc Institute),
    a StripedHyena 2 autoregressive model run via the Vortex inference engine. Pre-trained 7B weights are baked into the image and 
    loaded directly (no download at runtime). Requires an NVIDIA GPU, ideally H100s.

    Endpoints:
      POST /predict   — submit sequences + prediction_tasks, receive predictions
      GET  /help      — this Predictor metadata (predictor_help_message.json)
      GET  /formats   — supported request/response wire formats (JSON, MessagePack)

    Support scripts:
      - predictor_RestAPI.py         — Flask REST API and request orchestration
      - evo2_utils.py                — model loading + point/track prediction logic
      - config.py                    — container-aware Predictor versioning
      - schema_validation.py         — request payload validation and preprocessing
      - error_checking_functions.py  — standardized error classes and checks
      - predictor_content_handler.py — JSON / MessagePack content negotiation
      - predictor_help_message.json  — Predictor metadata served via /help

    Run the container (GPU required, no Matcher, yet):

        apptainer run --nv --containall evo2_predictor.sif 172.xx.xx.xxx 5000

    Arguments:
      1. HOST:  IP address or hostname for the Predictor to bind to
      2. PORT:  Port number the Predictor listens on